cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use carpool or its measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "carpool: many agent tasks, one verified request"
authors:
  - name: "carpool contributors"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nmayp/carpool"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
version: "0.3.0"
keywords:
  - llm
  - agents
  - token cost
  - batching
  - claude code
  - mcp
abstract: >-
  carpool puts independent LLM tasks into one request with stable IDs, checks every answer against its
  cited source, and redoes only the failures. On Claude it measured about 80% lower cost per accepted answer
  than one lean call per task (93-96% lower than one agent call per task), with zero regressions on two task sets.
